Notebook[{
Cell["InfraSceneHighlight", "Title",ExpressionUUID->"fc7ff1c3-f8b4-40d0-98e2-ee4e463195cb"],

Cell["[LLM Generated]", "Subtitle",ExpressionUUID->"c9408e51-0010-45db-9eba-fd46b4c89673"],

Cell["\<\
InfraSceneHighlight[g, multiObjects] renders a list of multi-objects \
diffusely on graph g, with intensity scaling by overlap within each object \
and color-blending across objects. InfraSceneHighlight[g, obj] is the \
single-object shortcut for InfraSceneHighlight[g, {obj}]. Each entry is \
auto-classified by representation; explicit Infra* wrappers force the \
intended semantics. Per-object style overrides via `entry -> color`, `entry \
-> Directive[dirs]`, `Style[entry, dirs__]`, or `entry -> {opts...}` with a \
flat option list auto-sorted into vertex (VertexStyle / VertexSize / \
VertexShapeFunction), edge (EdgeStyle / EdgeShapeFunction), and per-object \
diffusion (\"OpacityRange\" / \"ThicknessRange\" / \"PointSizeRange\") \
channels. A bare directive routes by family (thickness/dashing to edges, \
point-size to vertices, color/opacity to both) and overrides the matching \
diffusion range; use AbsolutePointSize[n] for a constant on-screen point \
size. Options: \"OpacityRange\", \"ThicknessRange\", \"PointSizeRange\".\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"7ad7b782-1bd0-4d9b-b7c9-99c30ccf50df"],

Cell["Setup", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"2c7f8747-3d78-4f1f-8a10-ac29abdf28ec"],

Cell["Load the paclet.", "CodeText",ExpressionUUID->"b6041a06-4ca1-4e3f-b5fd-c4725c96f98d"],

Cell[BoxData[
 RowBox[{"Needs", "[", "\"\<WolframInstitute`SyntheticInfrageometry`\>\"", 
  "]"}]], "Code",
 InitializationCell->
  True,ExpressionUUID->"fde24c4e-b01a-4a3a-b1b0-118beb95d2e3"],

Cell["Related Guides", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"07801f9b-0e82-4829-8c8a-75fb18b987ba"],

Cell["VisualizationGuide", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"56d93ac6-cc52-40f0-bc12-0d02aac67802"],

Cell["SyntheticInfrageometryGuide", "Item",ExpressionUUID->"d2ecf6ad-0c50-4da6-9c3f-b6f7b813e0e3"]
},
